---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { AUTHOR_NAME } from '../../data/site-config';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title="Editorial Policy of Canada Processing Times 2026: Sources" description="How Canada Processing Times writes its 2026 pages: IRCC’s published files only, every figure read by a script and dated, estimates labelled with their method, no consultant money." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Editorial policy' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Editorial policy</h1>
    <h2>What counts as a source</h2>
    <p>IRCC’s published files and pages on canada.ca, the Citizenship Act on the Justice Laws website, and copies of IRCC’s files kept by the Internet Archive, cited with their capture date. A news article, a forum post or another site can point us to a change; we publish it only after reading IRCC’s own figure. Times reported by applicants are not used.</p>
    <h2>How a figure reaches a page</h2>
    <p>A script reads each IRCC file, keeps the update date IRCC wrote in it and the date it was read, and adds the reading to the archive. Pages and calculators read those files; nobody types a time into a page. When a file cannot be read, the previous one is kept and pages show the IRCC date actually read.</p>
    <h2>Estimates</h2>
    <p>A decision date is always called an estimate, with its method linked. Nothing in the archive is interpolated: a week with no copy of IRCC’s file has no figure.</p>
    <h2>Independence</h2>
    <p>{AUTHOR_NAME} receives nothing from consultants, law firms, schools, recruiters or any other business that serves applicants, and the pages carry no affiliate links. The site is not linked to IRCC or any public body and does not present itself as one.</p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>A reported error is checked against IRCC’s file; if we were wrong, the page is corrected the same day. Write through the <a href={route('contact', lang)}>contact page</a>.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
